    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Boxing matches were very popular in England two hundred years ago.",
      "translation": "200年前，拳击比赛在英国非常流行。",
      "startTime": 18.59,
      "endTime": 23.51,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "boxing",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "拳击"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "In those days, boxers fought with bare fists for prize money.",
      "translation": "在那时，拳击手们为了争夺奖金而赤手空拳地搏斗。",
      "startTime": 23.52,
      "endTime": 28.92,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "bare",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "赤裸的"
          },
          {
            "word": "fist",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "拳头"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Because of this, they were known as 'prizefighters'.",
      "translation": "因此，他们被称为“职业拳击手”。",
      "startTime": 28.93,
      "endTime": 33.26,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "prizefighter",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "职业拳击手"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "However, boxing was very crude, for there were no rules and a prizefighter could be seriously injured or even killed during a match.",
      "translation": "然而，当时的拳击非常粗野，因为没有任何规则，职业拳击手在比赛中可能受重伤甚至丧命。",
      "startTime": 33.27,
      "endTime": 44.93,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "crude",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "粗野的，未加工的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "One of the most colourful figures in boxing history was Daniel Mendoza, who was born in 1764.",
      "translation": "拳击史上最引人注目的的人物之一是丹尼尔·门多萨，他出生于1764年。",
      "startTime": 44.94,
      "endTime": 53.55,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "colourful",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "丰富多彩的"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "The use of gloves was not introduced until 1860, when the Marquis of Queensberry drew up the first set of rules.",
      "translation": "直到1860年昆斯伯里侯爵制定了第一套规则，才开始使用手套。",
      "startTime": 53.56,
      "endTime": 62.62,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "glove",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "手套"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Though he was technically a prizefighter, Mendoza did much to change crude prizefighting into a sport, for he brought science to the game.",
      "translation": "虽然从技术上讲，他是一个职业拳击手，但门多萨为将粗野的职业拳击变为一项运动做了大量工作，因为他将科学带入了这项比赛。",
      "startTime": 62.63,
      "endTime": 73.7,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "technically",
            "pos": "adv.",
            "meaning": "技术上"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "In his day, Mendoza enjoyed tremendous popularity.",
      "translation": "在他那个时代，门多萨享有极高的声誉。",
      "startTime": 73.71,
      "endTime": 78.4,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "tremendous",
            "pos": "adj.",
            "meaning": "巨大的"
          },
          {
            "word": "popularity",
            "pos": "n.",
            "meaning": "名声，流行"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "He was adored by rich and poor alike.",
      "translation": "富人和穷人都同样崇拜他。",
      "startTime": 78.41,
      "endTime": 81.93,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "adore",
            "pos": "v.",
            "meaning": "崇拜，爱慕"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "Mendoza rose to fame swiftly after a boxing match when he was only fourteen years old.",
      "translation": "门多萨在14岁时的一次拳击比赛后迅速成名。",
      "startTime": 81.94,
      "endTime": 88.41,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
          {
            "word": "swiftly",
            "pos": "adv.",
            "meaning": "迅速地"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "Narrator",
      "text": "This attracted the attention of Richard Humphries who was then the most eminent boxer in England.",
      "translation": "这引起了当时英国最著名的拳击手里查德·汉弗莱斯的注意。",
      "startTime": 88.42,
      "endTime": 95.86,
      "analysis": {
        "words": [
